An interesting observation regarding past tense jailbreaks for other languages. If verbs don’t have tenses (like in Chinese), this seems to effectively reduce the attack surface :-)
Quoting @alc_anthro
@joefeng2000 I mean "past tense" works very differently in Chinese languages, right? There's no conjugation. It's temporal markers. Maybe that has something to do with it?

